+/*!
+   \fn double QCborStreamReader::toNumber() const
+   \since 6.13
+
+   Returns the numeric value of the current element as a \c double, whichever
+   CBOR numeric type it was encoded as: unsigned or negative integer, or
+   half-, single- or double-precision floating point.
+
+   Integers whose absolute value exceeds 2\sup{53} may not be exactly
+   representable as a \c double and are rounded to the nearest representable
+   value. Unlike toInteger(), this function does not overflow for integers
+   outside the range of \c qint64. Floating point values, including
+   infinities and NaN, are converted without loss.
+
+   This function does not perform any other type conversions, including from
+   booleans, CBOR tags (such as QCborKnownTags::PositiveBignum) or strings.
+   Therefore, it may only be called if isNumber() is true; calling it in any
+   other condition is an error.
